# Sharlie Easy Flow

Read `AGENTS.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` before structural edits.

- Node kinds are `agent` and `human`. Pipeline JSON stays version 1. `normalizePipeline` drops legacy skill nodes and attachment edges, and drops old agent prompt, `customModelId`, and human notes on load. Missing `agentPath`, `agentName`, `effort`, and `effortParamId` become empty strings. There is no skill node, no prompt field, and no attachment edge kind in the written document. A new kind updates `src/modules/graph/types.ts`, `src/App.tsx` `nodeTypes`, `src/modules/graph/resolve.ts`, and `src/modules/runs/engine.ts` together.
- `resolvePipeline(doc)` is pure and does not read files. An agent step is `{ kind: "agent", nodeId, inputs, modelId, agentPath, agentName, effort, effortParamId }` and a human step is `{ kind: "human", nodeId, inputs }`. `inputs` lists the distinct sources of the edges into that node, in step order; a duplicate edge counts once. `agentName` is trimmed. `effort` and `effortParamId` are trimmed, and an empty `effort` means not chosen yet. At run time a blank effort becomes `medium` when the model lists it, otherwise the middle allowed value. The sent parameter id is the stored `effortParamId` when it is set, otherwise the catalog id for that model, otherwise `effort`. Models with no effort parameter send no params. An empty model id throws `GraphError` `Model id is empty`. Attachment edges still present throw `GraphError`. The cycle message remains `Cycle in pipeline`.
- An agent node stores `modelId`, `effort`, `effortParamId`, `agentPath`, and `agentName`. An empty `effort` means not chosen yet. An empty `effortParamId` means the parameter id was not stored. There is no custom model field. The model dropdown is empty and disabled until `GET /api/models` returns a non-empty list. That route returns `{ configured: false, models: [] }` when `CURSOR_API_KEY` is missing, and only `listModels` results when the key is set. There is no preset fallback.
- `GET /api/agents` lists `.md` files directly in `%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/agents`. `POST /api/agents/browse` opens a native file dialog and returns the chosen `.md` path, name, and description. The node can also select one of the scanned agents. The file is not copied.
- On run, agents run in `<workspace>/<id>/`. The engine resolves `agentPath` with `resolveAgentPath` before calling the runner. An empty path stays empty. An absolute path stays as it is. A relative path is resolved against the workflow folder. The instruction is the markdown body with YAML frontmatter stripped when present. `applyCatalog` prefixes the enabled skill/rule catalog onto the first send only. A missing path or unreadable file fails the step before the SDK is called.
- A node starts only when every input is satisfied (agent `done`, human `approved`). Independent agents run in parallel, up to 3; parallel agents must work on different files. Upstream text comes only from connected inputs; a human input passes on the outputs of the agents it reviewed.
- Human nodes have no notes field. Approve, Redo, and Decline remain. Decline stops the whole run. Redo all re-sends every agent the human reviews; Redo one (`redoNodeId`) re-sends one. Redo increments that agent's retry and resends its file body on its own runner, with no catalog and no feedback wrapper. Decisions carry the human `nodeId`.
- Skills, rules, and MCP servers are an app-wide library, not canvas nodes. Scan is read-only and limited to `%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/skills` (`SKILL.md`), `%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/rules` (`.md` and `.mdc`), and `%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/mcp.json`. Workspace `.cursor` and plugins are not scanned. The dashboard does not author those files.
- Import is by browse. `POST /api/library/browse` opens a native folder dialog for a skill and resolves the `SKILL.md` directly inside the chosen folder, or a file dialog for `.mdc` or `.md` rules. Both dialogs allow more than one pick. `POST /api/library/import` takes one `path` or a `paths` list and records each absolute path in `data/library/imports.json` (`{ skills: string[], rules: string[] }`). The file is not copied. Remove forgets that path only. Imported rows use source `import`. A path that is already in the Cursor scan stays a single cursor row. MCP servers come only from the user `mcp.json`. `data/library/` also holds `selection.json` and is gitignored. Each workflow is saved at `<workspace>/<id>/.sharlie/workflow.json`. The folder name is the pipeline id. `data/app/` is gitignored.
- List APIs never return MCP env or header values. `loadEnabledMcpConfigs` is server-side and includes env. Do not log secrets or `CURSOR_API_KEY`. The key is stored in Windows Credential Manager, not in `.env`. Settings returns `{ configured }`.
- Enabled skills and rules still become a catalog (name, description, file path). The agent is told to read a file only when the description matches. Redo does not include the catalog again.
- Enabled MCP servers are passed to `Agent.create` as `mcpServers`. `local.settingSources` is `[]`. Ambient Cursor settings are not loaded.
- Only `src/modules/cursor/adapter.ts` may import `@cursor/sdk`. `src/modules/cursor/mcpServers.ts` maps configs and does not import the SDK.
- `GET /api/files` refuses paths outside the workspace, the workspace `.env`, and `data/library/mcp.json`. Library bodies go through `GET /api/library/body`.
- Library UI is a top-bar modal (`LibraryModal`), not a node.
- Do not add UI test suites. New parse, resolve, human-gate, library, or agent-file behavior needs a `node:test` file under `tests/`.
- `npm test` lists `tests/skills.test.ts`, `tests/graph.test.ts`, `tests/human-gate.test.ts`, `tests/schedule.test.ts`, `tests/run-engine.test.ts`, `tests/library.test.ts`, `tests/mcp-servers.test.ts`, `tests/agents.test.ts`, `tests/workspace.test.ts`, `tests/pipelines-storage.test.ts`, `tests/sharlie.test.ts`, `tests/sharlie-import.test.ts`, `tests/workflow-health.test.ts`, `tests/credentials.test.ts`, and `tests/agent-node-defaults.test.ts` explicitly so Windows does not depend on shell globbing.

## File map

- `server/index.ts` and `server/routes/` — HTTP API. `server/routes/library.ts` is the library API. `server/routes/agents.ts` lists and browses agent files. `server/routes/files.ts` is workspace preview.
- `src/modules/graph/resolve.ts` and `src/modules/graph/types.ts` — pipeline resolution and version 1 shapes (`agent`, `human`, execution edges).
- `src/modules/storage/pipelines.ts` — saved graphs, `normalizePipeline`, and `<workspace>/<id>/.sharlie/workflow.json`.
- `src/modules/runs/engine.ts`, `src/modules/runs/schedule.ts`, and `src/modules/runs/humanGate.ts` — dependency-driven run, parallel agents, catalog on the first send, agent file body on redo, and human decisions.
- `src/modules/cursor/adapter.ts` and `src/modules/cursor/models.ts` — runner and model id trimming. `src/modules/cursor/mcpServers.ts` maps MCP configs.
- `src/modules/agents/agentFile.ts` — user-level `.md` agent discovery and instruction text.
- `src/modules/skills/parseSkill.ts` and `src/modules/skills/scanSkills.ts` — markdown parsing and user-level `SKILL.md` discovery.
- `src/modules/library/` — scan, selection, imports, `applyCatalog`, and `loadEnabledMcpConfigs`.
- `src/modules/artifacts/track.ts` — file diffs.
- `src/App.tsx` and `src/modules/canvas/` — the canvas UI. `LibraryModal` is the library screen.
